Bugfix: Make the text of disabled controls readable

The label of a disabled input, button or text area was drawn in a grey that
reached 2.35:1 against its own surface, and the label beside such a field
2.85:1 against the page. The contrast requirement exempts inactive controls, so
neither was a violation, but a control whose label cannot be deciphered is
still information while it is switched off.

Both now use the muted text colour this interface already carries elsewhere,
which reaches 6.20:1 and 7.53:1. The muted fill is unchanged, so a disabled
control still reads as disabled.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 1.4.3
